{"_id":"c0c6861856b2c777","name":"First One's Free","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You can give away your product to build Rep during downtime. 1 Rep costs 1 unit.","class":"Dealers","class_default":"Dealers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"082e0591b02da6aa","name":"First Rate","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Your merchandise is exquisite. Gain potency when you Sway or Consort with those hooked on your product. When you deal with a crew or faction, the GM will tell you who among them is already hooked (one, a few, many, or all).","class":"Dealers","class_default":"Dealers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b3853b01ad6b7cfb","name":"On Retainer","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You have an expert lawyer representing your crew. Their Quality is equal to crew Tier +2. When you take the Reduce Heat downtime action, you can have your lawyer roll their Quality instead. When you take the rap, your Wanted Level counts as one lower for the purposes of sentencing.","class":"Dealers","class_default":"Dealers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"42da55bdaacc1319","name":"Cat and Mouse","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"The GM will tell you about any special Mandates investigating your crew, and put their clocks on the table from now on. You get +2d to the engagement roll against any raids (Mandates or otherwise).","class":"Dealers","class_default":"Dealers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"2b03f1c035115344","name":"Field Testing","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You can prepare a special cut of your product for use during a score. Choose an effect: healing (clear level 1 harm), exhilarating (clear 1 Stress), calming (social potency), enlightening (increase result level on gather information). Each costs 1 unit of product, takes 1 load, and is consumed after use.","class":"Dealers","class_default":"Dealers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"cd6f33244fcad0f8","name":"Payment in Kind","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You can use units to purchase crew upgrades. 1 crew upgrade costs 5 units (so a new cohort would cost 10 units).","class":"Dealers","class_default":"Dealers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b57ed096e5fea781","name":"Benefactor","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you take this ability, the crew immediately receives 4 stacks. Whenever you advance your Tier, it costs half the stacks it normally would. Who’s backing you? Why do they help you?","class":"","class_default":"","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a49d0ffc67c5d161","name":"Versatile","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Choose a special ability from another crew (can be taken more than once).","class":"","class_default":"","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"0cace355accc36cd","name":"Take the Shot","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When any PC takes the decisive action to eliminate a key target, they get +1d.","class":"Hit Squad","class_default":"Hit Squad","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"0036fca883421d33","name":"Under the Radar","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you kill someone during a score, you can take 2 Stress so that it doesn’t count towards Heat afterwards. How does your crew avoid the Death Radar?","class":"Hit Squad","class_default":"Hit Squad","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"a76d127ebfdc7871","name":"Chameleons","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Take +1d to the engagement roll for stealth or deception approaches. When you subdue someone and don their outfit, the disguise has increased effect.","class":"Hit Squad","class_default":"Hit Squad","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"2e683f83955d98f3","name":"Cold Storage","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Every crew member can always find a convenient place to hide a body near to hand. Take 1 Stress to hide the body in the resonance field instead (it will rematerialize after a few hours).","class":"Hit Squad","class_default":"Hit Squad","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ea4ac7646289bd37","name":"Loopers","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Your crew is caught in an anomaly, and regularly experiences time loops where events are replayed. Usually you don’t retain memory between loops, but you can jump loops with some effort. Take 4 Stress after any action roll to roll it again, and take the best result between the two rolls. The second roll uses the exact same number of dice (pushes, assists, etc.). You can choose to do this after the GM has announced the consequences, but not after any resistance rolls.","class":"Hit Squad","class_default":"Hit Squad","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"118b8702a92dc42a","name":"Professionals","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you keep an operation quiet or make it look like an accident, you get half the Rep value of the target (round up) instead of zero. When you end downtime with zero Heat, take +1 Rep.","class":"Hit Squad","class_default":"Hit Squad","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"f1ed7f15df9fe83c","name":"Sympathizers","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"The common citizenry of your home ground, and any turf you hold, are sympathetic to you and your cause. You can consider them allies (status +3). When asked, they will: give you shelter or a place to hide, redirect Bluecoats or other enemies, or give you other aid if they can.","class":"Militants","class_default":"Militants","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c56bdaef781d2344","name":"Mutual Aid","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You can lend support to one allied faction, and their Tier counts as one higher as long as you do. Your crew gets one free downtime action to work one of that faction’s long-term project clocks, if you wish. You can switch support once per downtime.","class":"Militants","class_default":"Militants","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"99758129da903eca","name":"Guerrillas","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When the target of a score is two or more Tier higher than you, take no penalty to the engagement roll, and gain +2 Rep after the score (whether you were successful or not).","class":"Militants","class_default":"Militants","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5e66a3e155afd6ba","name":"On the Side of the Oppressed","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You loudly and openly oppose the Bluecoats and their authoritarianism. You may count each Wanted Level as if it were turf.","class":"Militants","class_default":"Militants","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5a2cca31e9664e86","name":"Absolute Commitment","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You have all sworn solemn vows of service to the cause. You get +1d to resistance rolls.","class":"Militants","class_default":"Militants","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9747695c977d95a3","name":"Revolutionaries","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you’re at war (-3 faction status), your crew does not suffer -1 hold and PCs still get two downtime activities, instead of just one.","class":"Militants","class_default":"Militants","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d3b177adc8a38740","name":"Stunt Riders","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"The first time one of the crew’s signature stunts is performed during a score, take +2d and increased effect. Choose one to start with. The crew masters an additional signature stunt each time you take this ability. You can do any of these stunts even if they’re not a signature, but don’t get bonus dice etc.","class":"Racers","class_default":"Racers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"fff85af8a858b78b","name":"Custom Ride","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Create one of your vehicles (autopod, autocycle, boat, etc.) as a cohort (use 1-2 vehicle edges and an equal number of flaws). Its Quality is equal to your Tier +1. It includes a driver, if needed.","class":"Racers","class_default":"Racers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"0778a573e952c058","name":"Escape Velocity","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"One of the crew’s vehicles is fitted with a device that activates at a specific speed. This requires filling an 8-segment acceleration clock during the score. When the clock is filled and the vehicle hits the target speed, choose an effect: break the laws of gravity—create a tear in reality—travel into the resonance field— travel backward or forward through time.","class":"Racers","class_default":"Racers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"920e9172f07c00ac","name":"The Family Takes a Cut","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Before payout for a smuggling or hijacking score, the crew can skim the goods for +4 stacks. The GM will tick a clock.","class":"Racers","class_default":"Racers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"35076a3889e4dffb","name":"Bring Them In","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"As long as you’re not currently fighting them (e.g. you’re at war), you can turn even the most bitter of enemies into family. This requires a long-term project—6 segments to turn them into a crew contact, 10 segments to turn them into a cohort or PC (your choice). If they become a PC, create them as normal, with bonus action dots and abilities each equal to their Tier, and any deadlocks at the GM’s discretion. Their faction’s relationship to your crew does not change.","class":"Racers","class_default":"Racers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"9a86fa488eb33917","name":"Speed Demons","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you go into conflict aboard a vehicle, you gain increased effect for vehicle damage and speed. If the vehicle has armor, you can use it for your own protection.","class":"Racers","class_default":"Racers","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"83da9c2195ddb348","name":"Synchronized Watches","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You may use assists or setup actions with any crew member, regardless of the distance separating you. When you perform a group action, you may count multiple 6s from different rolls as a critical success.","class":"Shadows","class_default":"Shadows","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"202d70c7c63fc355","name":"Thieves With a Code","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you complete a score with no deaths having occurred, gain +1 faction status with the local citizenry.","class":"Shadows","class_default":"Shadows","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"70fde22f10d15124","name":"Sleepy Time","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Everyone on the crew adds tranquilizer rounds (0 load, compatible with any firearm) to their playbook items.","class":"Shadows","class_default":"Shadows","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"6ef44f28e1f1b018","name":"Don't Forget the Duffel Bag","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Once per score, the crew can flashback to an Acquire Asset roll with +2d. Both the flashback and the downtime activity are free.","class":"Shadows","class_default":"Shadows","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"ffdf4d6dddce895c","name":"Echo Safe House","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"The crew has access to a safe house in the resonance field. It can be accessed once per score, from anywhere. The door always returns to the same place it was entered from. Use it as a hiding place, to reequip, repair, or just take a breather. Any PCs who enter gain +1 load. One PC may clear all level 1 harm via emergency medical supplies there. Note that time still passes in the outside world.","class":"Shadows","class_default":"Shadows","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"5fdc1d9d5fe4349f","name":"Black Bag Operations","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you execute a clandestine infiltration, you get +1d to the engagement roll. You may attempt to install surveillance equipment during a score on any faction’s turf. So long as the wire remains in place, take +1d on any future gather information rolls related to that faction. The GM may make a fortune roll with the faction’s Tier to see if they notice the bug and remove it during personal business.","class":"Shadows","class_default":"Shadows","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"aea25b31851375d0","name":"Enlightened","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You get +1d to resistance rolls against paranormal threats and consequences. You get +1d to healing rolls when you have paranormal harm.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"07fa7a062810126b","name":"Commune","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You may use teamwork with any crew member, regardless of the distance separating you. By taking 1 Stress, your projected thoughts are heard by every crew member as telepathic communication.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"deb4f1346ebc50a9","name":"Best Intentions","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"If every PC vows not to kill anyone before a score, take +1d to the engagement roll. The first time each PC takes an action that might kill someone if it’s successful (whether intentional by the PC or not), they take +1d and potency. If you all keep the vow, the crew marks 1 xp.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"41b071f2571cc43c","name":"Zeal","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Every PC gets +1d and potency when they evangelize about the Utopian Vision.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c1d5204087dd8009","name":"-------","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"ONCE YOU HAVE DESCENDED TO THE SECOND CIRCLE, YOU MAY CHOOSE:","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"de61adc546061dbf","name":"True Believers","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Your cohorts will undertake any service, no matter how dangerous or strange. They gain +1d to rolls against enemies of the Utopian Vision.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"cefbd1ea2a961b22","name":"Altered States","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Each PC gains an additional vice: Ritual Hedonism. When you indulge this vice, you don't overindulge if you clear excess Stress. In addition, your ecstatic visions of the future mean you can perform one flashback for free.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c1d5204087dd8009","name":"-------","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"ONCE YOU HAVE DESCENDED TO THE THIRD CIRCLE, YOU MAY CHOOSE:","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"d743945e25d0d8c5","name":"For the Greater Good","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"A human sacrifice removes the Stress cost for any paranormal experiment you perform, and such sacrifices performed in your base do not trigger the Death Radar or generate Heat.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"da0cb2811825a0fa","name":"This Is Fine","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"If every PC works together (group action), you can summon a denizen of your Utopian Vision into this reality: a Class V Resonance Entity.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"c1d5204087dd8009","name":"-------","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"ONCE YOU HAVE DESCENDED TO THE FINAL CIRCLE, YOU MAY CHOOSE:","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"7efca895ac49a5f8","name":"Remember the Forgotten","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You can now communicate with the entity who created your Utopian Vision (a “god”?). Tread carefully.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"05586c5464dce6d4","name":"Paradise Manifest","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you take this advance, your base and the area around transforms into a small fragment of your utopia, manifest in this reality. Take +2d to the engagement roll for any raids. All crew members gain potency when acting in the base and its surrounds, and all downtime actions conducted in the base get +1 result level. This will attract significant attention from Section 6 and other high-Tier factions.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"fb2c9807757f4f19","name":"We No Longer Play By Your Rules","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you take this advance, immediately pick two more advances.","class":"Utopians","class_default":"Utopians","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"1a7e229ca7eb0369","name":"As Good as Your Word","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"You may spend rep as coin in downtime actions. Vigilantes gain Obligation as a second vice.","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"404641565b1ef523","name":"Avengers","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Each PC may add +1 action rating to Hunt, Prowl, or Command (up to a max rating of 3).","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"caea1fe0cded8c7d","name":"Thorn in your Side","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"When you use Stealth or Assault plans against a higher Tier faction, your Tier counts as +1.","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"381a4218d0ff2550","name":"Misdirection","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"At the end of a score, you may sacrifice half the rep gained to make another faction lose status with your target instead of your crew. How do you pin it on someone else?","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"b4f57bebc4fb526b","name":"Uncanny Preparation","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Twice per session during a Desperate action, improve your effect or position. Describe a flashback that gives you the advantage now (setup action).","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3eb246a6d6b39391","name":"Moral Compass","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Each PC gains an additional xp trigger: You fulfilled an obligation at a cost to you or the crew.","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"8a499dad27905dd6","name":"Favors","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"Spend one rep and describe how one of your contacts is put out to help you. Everyone in your crew gets one dot in an action your contact is skilled in for this score.","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
{"_id":"3bbd0c87e5b7dc95","name":"Roots","type":"crew_ability","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"description":"During downtime one of your contacts or cohorts may take a downtime action to acquire an asset, reduce heat, or recover.","class":"Vigilantes","class_default":"Vigilantes","price":"1","purchased":false},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"permission":{"default":0},"flags":{}}
